.TH MMENU 1 "October 2026" "mmenu" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mmenu \- interactive terminal menu and batch filter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mmenu
.RI [ PROMPT ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B mmenu
.BR --filter " " QUERY
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mmenu
reads newline-delimited options from standard input. Interactive mode lets the
user search and select an option; the selected record is written to standard
output. Batch filtering with
.B --filter
prints matching records without opening a terminal.
.PP
Interactive mode can display records while input is still arriving. Matching is
ASCII-case-insensitive by default. The selected record is printed unless
.B -t
requests its zero-based input index.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR -f " " QUERY ", " --filter " " QUERY
Filter all input records without opening the interactive menu. Also accepts
.B --filter=QUERY.
.TP
.B --fuzzy
Match query characters as an ordered subsequence and rank matches by score.
.TP
.B --exact
Match complete records byte-for-byte, case-sensitively.
.TP
.BR -x ", " --extended
Enable query expressions: whitespace-separated AND terms, | for OR groups,
! for inverse terms, a leading apostrophe for contiguous terms, ^ for prefixes,
and $ for suffixes.
.TP
.BR -i ", " --ignore-case
Use ASCII-case-insensitive matching (the default).
.TP
.BR +i ", " --no-ignore-case
Use ASCII-case-sensitive matching.
.TP
.B --smart-case
Ignore case unless the query contains an ASCII uppercase letter.
.TP
.BR -v ", " --invert-match
In batch mode, print records that do not match. Requires
.BR --filter .
.TP
.B --no-sort
With
.BR --fuzzy ,
preserve input order instead of ranking matches.
.TP
.B --tiebreak=KEYS
Order equal-score fuzzy matches by comma-separated keys: length, begin, end,
chunk, pathname, and index. Requires
.BR --fuzzy .
.TP
.B --multi
Enable multi-selection. Tab toggles an option; Enter prints selected records
in original input order. If none were toggled, Enter selects the current option.
.TP
.B --cycle
Wrap Up/Down navigation at either end of the result list.
.TP
.B --disabled
Keep all options visible while editing the query.
.TP
.B --query QUERY
Prefill the interactive query.
.TP
.B --layout MODE
Set the interactive layout to
.BR default ,
.BR reverse ,
or
.BR reverse-list .
The latter keeps the query at the top and puts the first option at the bottom.
.TP
.B --reverse
Place the query row at the bottom. Alias for
.BR --layout=reverse .
.TP
.B --reverse-list
Keep the query at the top and render the first option at the bottom. Alias for
.BR --layout=reverse-list .
.TP
.B --height N
Limit the interactive option list to N rows.
.TP
.B --height PCT%
Use the specified percentage (1–100) of available option rows.
.TP
.B --preview COMMAND
Show command output for the highlighted record. The placeholders
.BR {} ,
.BR {index} ,
and
.B {query}
expand to the selected record, its zero-based input index, and the query.
Placeholder values are shell-quoted, but the command itself is executed by the
shell. Use only trusted commands.
.TP
.B --read0
Read NUL-delimited input records instead of newline-delimited records.
.TP
.B --print0
Terminate output records with NUL instead of newline.
.TP
.B -t
Print zero-based indexes instead of records. In interactive mode, the legacy
second positional argument
.B t
or
.B true
has the same effect.
.TP
.B --nth SPEC
Search only the selected 1-based fields or ranges, such as
.BR 1,3 ,
.BR 2..4 ,
or
.BR 1,-1 .
.TP
.B --with-nth SPEC
Display only selected fields in interactive mode while preserving original
records for output.
.TP
.B --accept-nth SPEC
Output only selected fields from accepted records.
.TP
.BR -d " " REGEX ", " --delimiter " " REGEX
Split fields using a POSIX extended regular expression. Requires
.BR --nth ,
.BR --with-nth ,
or
.BR --accept-nth .
The expression must not match an empty string.
.TP
.B --format FORMAT
In batch mode, expand
.B {}
to the record,
.B {index}
to its original zero-based index, and
.B {query}
to the query. Requires
.BR --filter ;
cannot be combined with
.BR -t .
.TP
.B --bind-up KEY
.TQ
.B --bind-down KEY
.TQ
.B --bind-accept KEY
.TQ
.B --bind-cancel KEY
.TQ
.B --bind-toggle KEY
.TQ
.B --bind-backspace KEY
Add a printable ASCII key alias for the specified action. Use
.B space
for the Space key. Toggle binding requires
.BR --multi .
.SH EXAMPLES
Select a file and open it with less:
.PP
.nf
find . -type f | mmenu "Open: " | xargs -d '\\n' -r less
.fi
.PP
Print matching C files:
.PP
.nf
find . -type f | mmenu --filter .c
.fi
.PP
Use fuzzy matching with a prefilled query and reverse-list layout:
.PP
.nf
find . -type f | mmenu --fuzzy --query main --layout reverse-list
.fi
.PP
Print the indexes of matching records:
.PP
.nf
mmenu --filter needle -t < files.txt
.fi
.PP
Filter NUL-delimited records and preserve NUL output:
.PP
.nf
printf 'alpha\\0beta\\0' | mmenu --read0 --filter beta --print0
.fi
.PP
Show file information for the highlighted record:
.PP
.nf
find . -type f | mmenu --preview 'file {}'
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns zero on successful completion. Invalid command-line arguments and
runtime errors return a nonzero status.
.SH NOTES
Requires a C compiler and the wide-character ncurses library at build time. The build driver probes for the platform's terminfo linker requirements; consumers linking the C API may need to add `-ltinfow` or `-ltinfo` after `-lncursesw`.
Preview commands execute through the shell; do not pass untrusted command text.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fzf (1),
.BR grep (1),
.BR find (1)
